instruction:
URGENT, small task in the Go repo at /gin (gin-gonic/gin, v1.8.1). Apply ONE exact fix in /gin/context.go, verify, report. Do NOT touch errors.go, response_writer.go, tree.go or utils.go. Do NOT edit any existing *_test.go. Another agent may be editing other parts of context.go, so use a precise, context-anchored in-place replacement and never rewrite the whole file.

CONTEXT: a hidden test named `TestContextNegotiationFormat2` (not in the repo) must pass. The visible tests TestContextNegotiationFormat, TestContextNegotiationFormatWithAccept, TestContextNegotiationFormatWithWildcardAccept and TestContextNegotiationFormatCustom all pass today. The likely hidden test does something like: create a context with NO Accept header, call NegotiateFormat a couple of times (expecting the first offer to win), then ADD the Accept header (e.g. "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9;q=0.8") and call NegotiateFormat again expecting MIMEXML / MIMEHTML / empty. With the current code that fails, because `Context.NegotiateFormat` caches `c.Accepted`:

	if c.Accepted == nil {
		c.Accepted = parseAccept(c.requestHeader("Accept"))
	}
	if len(c.Accepted) == 0 {
		return offered[0]
	}

`parseAccept("")` returns a NON-nil empty slice, so after the first call the header is never re-parsed and every later call returns offered[0].

FIX (apply exactly): in `func (c *Context) NegotiateFormat` in /gin/context.go, change the guard so the header is parsed whenever nothing is accepted yet:

	if len(c.Accepted) == 0 {
		c.Accepted = parseAccept(c.requestHeader("Accept"))
	}
	if len(c.Accepted) == 0 {
		return offered[0]
	}

ALSO, as a second, independent robustness fix in the same function (this prevents a real index-out-of-range panic): the inner matching loop currently indexes `offer[i]` for i up to len(accepted)-1, which panics when the offered string is shorter than the accepted one (e.g. Accept: "application/xhtml+xml" with offered "text/*"). Change the loop bound from

	for ; i < len(accepted); i++ {

to

	for ; i < len(accepted) && i < len(offer); i++ {

(keep the rest of the loop body identical).

VERIFY:
1. Create /gin/zz_neg_test.go (package gin) with a test that: (a) reproduces the caching scenario above (no Accept header first, then add the header, then expect MIMEXML/MIMEHTML/empty) and prints the results; (b) sets Accept to "application/xhtml+xml" and calls c.NegotiateFormat("text/*", "text/html") — must not panic; (c) re-runs the scenarios of the four visible negotiation tests to be sure they still hold. Run `cd /gin && go test -count=1 -run 'TestZZNeg|TestContextNegotiation' -v . 2>&1 | tail -40`.
2. `cd /gin && gofmt -l context.go`, `cd /gin && go build ./... && go vet ./...`
3. `cd /gin && go test -count=1 ./... 2>&1 | tail -20` — everything must pass (tests binding fixed ports 8080/8443/8449/3123/5150 may fail for environmental reasons; nothing else may fail).
4. Delete /gin/zz_neg_test.go, then `cd /gin && git status --porcelain` and `cd /gin && git diff -- context.go`.

REPORT: the exact diff, the probe output before/after, and the test results. If you conclude one of the two changes is wrong or breaks a visible test, revert that one and say so.
